 system","tags":["feminine","masculine"],"word":"ginecologista"}],"pos":"noun","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"In the last analysis, the fate of each individual woman rests in the hands of the gynaecologist.","ref":"1950, Moya Woodside, Sterilization in North Carolina: A Sociological and Psychological Study, University of North Carolina Press, page 56:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[82,95]],"id":"ccaa2523-6196-4337-8819-ea73e48664e5"},{"text":"Since there is an important bill under study today, we are asked to hope that a gynaecologist will sit on a therapeutic committee.","ref":"1969, Canadian House of Commons, Debates, Official Report, page 8287:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[80,93]],"id":"4754740d-49a2-4cc2-88be-6c5954d3d76b"},{"text":"During the past 5 years considerable interest has been shown by gynaecologists in the technique of laparoscopy (Steptoe, 1967; Cohen, 1970).","ref":"1972, The Australian and New Zealand Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology, volume 12, page 194:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[64,78]],"id":"1b52c48f-1440-4f94-876a-e6ba381b7849"},{"text":"According to the Bill, from the moment that the embryo insertion has been completed, the authority for the gynaecologist to have an embryo in his possession immediately and automatically ends.","ref":"1984, British House of Commons, Parliamentary debates (Hansard), page 345:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[107,120]],"id":"ef03eea3-fbfb-48c1-b6ea-67c682871b6c"},{"text":"Mr Shikuku: […]Was there any gynaecologist among those doctors?\nMr. Angatia: Mr. Speaker, Sir, there was a gynaecologist and also a midwife.","ref":"1995 October 31, Kenya National Assembly Official Record (Hansard), page 2287:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[0,11],[29,42],[64,76],[107,120]],"id":"2463d562-3da4-451e-9990-a2a1a3a7b534"},{"text":"2009, India Today, Volume 34, Issues 36-43, page 592,\nWith one of the highest birth rates across the world (22.69 births per 